<title>SPAIN: Santander cuts prime by 50 b.p. to 8 pct.</title>
<headline>Santander cuts prime by 50 b.p. to 8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Santander said on Friday that it cut its prime rate by 50 basis points to eight percent.</p>
<p>Earlier, the Bank of Spain cut its key money market rate to 6.25 percent from 6.75 percent, its seventh interest rate reduction of the year.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
